
FACE RECOGNITION MODEL COMPARISON
================================

Experiment: Pre-trained vs Partially Fine-tuned FaceNet
Evaluation date: 28 October 2026
Execution device: CPU

EVALUATION SETUP
----------------
Evaluation images selected: 240
Images with valid embeddings from both models: 236
Images where face detection failed: 4
Pair comparisons: 27,730
Same-identity pairs: 3,364
Different-identity pairs: 24,366

VERIFICATION RESULTS
--------------------
Model                  ROC-AUC    Average Precision
Pre-trained FaceNet    0.980838   0.958213
Fine-tuned FaceNet     0.961675   0.900969

OBSERVATION
-----------
The pre-trained FaceNet model achieved higher ROC-AUC and
average precision than the partially fine-tuned model in
this experiment.

Fine-tuning did not improve verification performance on
the selected high-quality evaluation subset.

LIMITATIONS
-----------
1. Results use a limited, high-quality evaluation subset.
2. Four evaluation images did not produce valid face embeddings.
3. The candidate split has not been fully verified for
   cross-quality near-duplicate leakage.
4. Pair comparisons are not statistically independent because
   multiple pairs share the same images.
5. Results do not establish performance on low-quality images.
6. The models use their own corresponding classifiers in the
   separate identity-classification experiment. That experiment
   is distinct from the verification experiment documented here.
7. Results should be treated as preliminary, not as proof of
   generalization to unseen people or real-world deployment.

REPRODUCIBILITY
---------------
Verification script:
src/compare_verification_models.py

Pair scores:
results/pre_post_verification_pair_scores.csv

Summary:
results/pre_post_verification_summary.csv

Figures:
results/pre_post_verification_roc.png
results/pre_post_verification_pr.png
results/pre_post_verification_similarity.png

Evaluation images were not used for gradient training in
this verification script. The integrity of the underlying
split remains subject to the leakage limitations above.
